<assembly xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/plugins/maven-assembly-plugin/assembly/1.1.3"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/plugins/maven-assembly-plugin/assembly/1.1.3
                              http://maven.apache.org/xsd/assembly-1.1.3.xsd">
  <!--
    Replaces the stock jar-with-dependencies descriptor for one reason: that one lets a
    dependency's plugins.config overwrite ours.

    ImageJ reads a single plugins.config from the root of each jar to build its menus. When a
    dependency ships one it lands at the same path as ours, and whichever the assembly unpacks
    last wins. That happened: the fast fitter was briefly a dependency, its file won, and the
    built jar advertised the Fast SMLM entries and none of TERRAPINS' own - the Workflow, Results
    Viewer and HAWK Stream commands simply did not appear. Silently, since an absent menu raises
    nothing and the build was perfectly happy.

    The fitter is now compiled from vendored sources (imagej/PROVENANCE.md) rather than resolved
    as an artifact, so no current dependency ships a plugins.config and the exclusion protects
    rather than repairs. Keep it. ThunderSTORM ships one too, and when it is bundled its entries
    must not be registered from inside this jar at all - a relocated copy appearing as a second
    ThunderSTORM in the menus would be worse than the original fault.

    So dependencies are unpacked with plugins.config excluded, and this module's own copy is the
    only one in the jar. It carries the fitter's entries too - see src/main/resources.
  -->
  <id>jar-with-dependencies</id>
  <formats>
    <format>jar</format>
  </formats>
  <includeBaseDirectory>false</includeBaseDirectory>
  <dependencySets>
    <dependencySet>
      <outputDirectory>/</outputDirectory>
      <useProjectArtifact>true</useProjectArtifact>
      <unpack>true</unpack>
      <scope>runtime</scope>
      <unpackOptions>
        <excludes>
          <exclude>plugins.config</exclude>
        </excludes>
      </unpackOptions>
    </dependencySet>
  </dependencySets>
  <fileSets>
    <!-- Our own plugins.config, added after the dependencies so nothing can shadow it. -->
    <fileSet>
      <directory>${project.basedir}/src/main/resources</directory>
      <outputDirectory>/</outputDirectory>
      <includes>
        <include>plugins.config</include>
      </includes>
    </fileSet>
  </fileSets>
</assembly>
